= Picking our enemies

Campaign materials cannot give equal weight to every conflict. Who should
Lewica present as its principal opponent?

[? if poland_enemy_focus != "No fixed enemy": The previous line named **[+
poland_enemy_focus +]**. A new choice will change which relationships and
voters bear the campaign's pressure. ?]

- @anti_democratic
- @far_right
- @pis
- @konf
- @capitalist
- @no_fixed_enemy

@anti_democratic
title: The anti-democratic right in PiS and Konfederacja
subtitle: A constitutional front improves liberal relations but closes channels to the whole right.
on-arrival: poland_enemy_focus = "the anti-democratic right"; pis_relation -= 5; konf_relation -= 8; ko_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 2; constitutional_restraint += 3; judicial_legitimacy += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; party_unity += 1; government_negotiation_hostility += 3 if government_party = "pis"; news_headline = "Lewica names the anti-democratic right as its principal enemy"

The line joins institutional defence to opposition coordination. It also lets
every PiS current claim that Lewica refuses to distinguish welfare policy from
constitutional capture.

- #poland_card_finish


@far_right
title: The radical right around Konfederacja, Braun and the street networks
subtitle: Concentrate fire beyond PiS; progressive organisers approve and PiS hostility eases slightly.
on-arrival: poland_enemy_focus = "the radical right"; konf_relation -= 12; pis_relation += 2; government_negotiation_hostility -= 2 if government_party = "pis"; far_right_agenda -= 3; party_system_konf_pull -= 2; civic_patriotism += 3; progressive_credibility += 3; progressives_dissent -= 2; young_support += 1; news_headline = "Lewica concentrates its campaign on the radical right"

The distinction contests Konfederacja's anti-system electorate without
pretending that PiS is democratic on every institutional question.

- #poland_card_finish


@pis
title: PiS alone—the governing apparatus and its whole record
subtitle: Opposition relations improve; PiS closes ranks and negotiations become more hostile.
on-arrival: poland_enemy_focus = "PiS"; pis_relation -= 12; ko_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 2; psl_relation += 1; government_negotiation_hostility += 6 if government_party = "pis"; united_right_cohesion += 3; progressive_credibility += 2; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "Lewica makes the PiS governing record its single campaign target"

The message is simple enough to repeat everywhere. It gives PiS solidarists no
reason to break publicly with their market and culture-war allies.

- #poland_card_finish


@konf
title: Konfederacja alone—the anti-social and anti-system right
subtitle: Compete for workers and younger voters; PiS relations improve at a cost to anti-PiS unity.
on-arrival: poland_enemy_focus = "Konfederacja"; konf_relation -= 15; pis_relation += 3; ko_relation -= 1; p2050_relation -= 1; far_right_agenda -= 4; party_system_konf_pull -= 3; labor_credibility += 2; young_support += 2; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "Lewica identifies Konfederacja as the anti-social right"

The campaign contests taxes, labour rights, housing and privatisation rather
than competing on Konfederacja's culture-war terrain. Liberal allies suspect a
deliberate opening toward PiS voters.

- #poland_card_finish


@capitalist
title: The capitalist parties—KO, Poland 2050 and PSL's market wing
subtitle: Relations with the liberal centre fall; PiS solidarists find more room to answer from the social side.
on-arrival: poland_enemy_focus = "the capitalist parties"; ko_relation -= 8; p2050_relation -= 6; psl_relation -= 4; pis_relation += 4; government_negotiation_hostility -= 3 if government_party = "pis"; pis_solidarist_share += 3; pis_market_hardliner_share -= 3; labor_credibility += 4; razem_dissent -= 4; progressives_dissent -= 2; barons_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Lewica turns its campaign against the capitalist centre"

The sharper class line pleases the socialist left and damages the relationships
most likely to produce a liberal-led cabinet. PiS can now compete by defending
its own social transfers instead of answering only from the right.

- #poland_card_finish


@no_fixed_enemy
title: Keep the campaign flexible
subtitle: No fixed enemy; preserve every channel and gain little definition.
on-arrival: poland_enemy_focus = "No fixed enemy"; public_trust += 1; media_capacity -= 1; issue_ownership -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica declines to organise its campaign around one enemy"

Every local organisation can choose its contrast. The national campaign gains
room to manoeuvre and loses a sentence that everyone can remember.

- #poland_card_finish
